From c8e1f49291e9b09d19d1b97d43593de6b5e8dc23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aamir <aamir@tallow-lang.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:52:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/27] Cargo.toml: declare `real-ml`, whose enabled branch is
 an honest refusal
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The feature was referenced by `#[cfg(feature = "real-ml")]` in
src/browser/ml/embeddings.rs but never declared, so that branch had never been
compiled and every build emitted two `unexpected_cfgs` warnings for a feature
Cargo did not define.

Declaring it is safe, and that was verified rather than assumed: the gated branch
does not attempt a candle loader — with `real-ml` on, `EmbeddingEngine::new`
returns a documented MlError ("real-ml is not shipped") instead of silently
falling back to the mock. Enabling it therefore cannot quietly substitute a
non-semantic engine for a semantic one.

Verified: default `cargo check --lib --bins` RC=0 with the warnings gone;
`cargo check --features real-ml` RC=0, so the branch compiles.

Also in this commit: stdlib/browser.tl's `StructuredData.extract` comment now says
which backend runs it. It claimed `// native:` in the file's established idiom
("implemented by the runtime, not in .tl"), which is true of the interpreter but
silent about the AOT backend having no lowering — so `tallow run` falls back and
`--require-native` refuses. Results are correct either way; the comment now says
so instead of leaving it to be inferred.
---
 Cargo.toml        | 8 ++++++++
 stdlib/browser.tl | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index d27c5b8..21d8c55 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -296,6 +296,14 @@ s3-storage = ["dep:object_store"]
 # src/browser/job_queue.rs). Requires a reachable Redis server; see
 # deploy/redis-backend.md for how to run a distributed Tallow cluster.
 redis-backend = ["dep:redis"]
+# `real-ml`: NOT SHIPPED. There is no candle-based loader in this build, so
+# enabling it cannot yield a real model — `EmbeddingEngine::new` returns a
+# documented `MlError` rather than silently falling back to the mock (a silent
+# fallback would let callers believe they got semantic embeddings when they did
+# not). Declared so the `#[cfg(feature = "real-ml")]` sites are legal — they
+# previously emitted `unexpected_cfgs` warnings for a feature Cargo did not
+# define — and so `--features real-ml` is an honest, testable switch.
+real-ml = []
 # Real Cranelift JIT backend (`src/codegen_cranelift.rs` + `src/jit.rs`).
 # OFF by default so a stock build stays dependency-light. When enabled, the
 # tracing JIT hooks the interpreter to hot-compile basic blocks to native
diff --git a/stdlib/browser.tl b/stdlib/browser.tl
index c196c47..6b1299e 100644
--- a/stdlib/browser.tl
+++ b/stdlib/browser.tl
@@ -440,6 +440,14 @@ struct StructuredData {
 /// Extract structured data (JSON-LD, OpenGraph) from HTML.
 fn structured_data_extract(html: String) -> StructuredData {
     // native: parses script[type="application/ld+json"] and meta[property^="og:"]
+    //
+    // Which engine: the interpreter reaches this through the `stdlib::browser`
+    // facade. The AOT native backend has NO lowering for this method, so
+    // `tallow run` falls back to the interpreter and `--require-native` refuses
+    // loudly rather than pretending. Results are correct either way; only the
+    // backend differs. (Binding `tallow_structured_data_extract` is the open
+    // P2.T1 item: it needs a native that builds the `%struct.StructuredData`
+    // layout, including the runtime representation of `[]String` and `Map`.)
 }
 
